---
title: Cinnamon Swirls
author: Jonathan Simmonds
cook time: 20 min
---

Preheat oven to 175°C.

On a floured surface roll out the @puff pastry{375%g} to measure 30x40 cm. Beat together the @butter{75%g}(half melted), @golden caster{75%g}, and @ground cinnamon{}(2%tsp) in a bowl, then spread over the pastry. Scatter with @sultanas{60%g} and then roll the rectangle from the short side to make a sausage. Chill for ~{15%minutes} until completely firm.

With a serrated knife cut into 16, 1.5cm slices. Lay flat-side down on a greased #baking sheet{} and press slightly so they spread a little. Chill for ~{20%minutes}.

Beat the @egg{1%medium} and @milk{2%tbsp} and brush over the pastry. Sprinkle with @golden caster{}(extra for sprinkling), and bake for ~{15-20%minutes}, until golden.

> Can be frozen before baking for up to a month. Bake from frozen, brushing with the egg mixture halfway through and sprinkling with sugar, until golden brown.
